    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 15th with an offensive outlook anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.53). **Yordan Alvarez** is our clear top-tier play against Jack Leiter; despite a neutral park factor, his elite 0.421 xwOBA and favorable platoon split make him a must-start anchor. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a massive boost due to the combination of a high-ceiling dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the opposing battery\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a prime environment for him to exploit the league\u2019s scarcity in stolen bases. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) also grades out strongly, benefiting from a soft matchup against Junk, where his ability to drive the ball keeps him in the upper echelon of our daily projections.\n\nWhile the core remains solid, we are navigating high-risk matchups at the top of the order, specifically regarding **Trea Turner** (53.83) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.46). Both face a tough test in Ashcraft, whose xERA of 3.52 is suppressing their raw power outputs. We are also keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Casey Schmitt**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Luke Raley**. **Casey Schmitt** represents an intriguing value play; if confirmed in the #3 hole, his +11% SP skill rating and positive platoon outlook against Civale make him an unexpected engine for the middle of our lineup. \n\nThe most difficult bench decision today involved **Carson Benge** (46.30). While **Carson Benge** holds a respectable projection buoyed by a prime leadoff spot, he narrowly missed the cut due to the sheer density of higher-efficiency options in our crowded outfield. We are prioritizing the stolen base upside of players like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Hyeseong Kim** to maximize our 5x5 category allocation. Managers should note that while **Dillon Dingler** (43.81) carries a sub-45 score, his placement in the #2 hole preserves his value despite a challenging matchup against Yesavage. With **Lars Nootbaar** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the current configuration maximizes our daily efficiency floor.",
